        "id": "R-privacy-1",
        "line": 11,
        "location": "src/logger.ts:3",
        "raisedBy": [
          "privacy"
        ],
        "recommendation": "The pattern only accepts ASCII letters on both sides of the `@`, and its first group needs an ASCII character right before the `@`. `logInfo(\"signup\", { user: \"josé@exemple.fr\" })` finds no match (the character before `@` is `é`) and writes `josé@exemple.fr` whole to the logs the hosting provider keeps 90 days — the very leak the proposal promises to stop (GDPR Art. 5(1)(c), Art. 32). Same for an internationalized domain (`ada@exämple.org`). Match on `\\S+@\\S+` (or Unicode classes with the `u` flag, `[\\p{L}\\p{N}._%+-]`) and add tests with an accented local part and an IDN domain.\n",
        "reported": true,
        "role": "privacy",
        "severity": "high",
        "status": "open",
